      "writtenOn": "2022-02-03T22:46:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "zmake coverage only builds and runs tests.\n\nOk, here is what might be nicer.\n\nMaybe what we need for consistency is:\n\n`configure [-b|--build] [-c|--coverage] [--test]` \u003d Configures cmake and optionally builds or runs test.\n`build [-c|--coverage]` \u003d Runs a configured project, and if not a test, and -c was specified generates the 0-line coverage zephyr.info file.\n`test [-c|--coverage]` \u003d Runs test, and if -c was specified generates lcov zephyr.info file.\n\nand \n\n`configureall [-b|--build] [-c|--coverage] [--test]` \u003d Same as configure but for all projects. If -c, merge zephyr.info files into build/zephyr/all_projects.info\n`buildall [-c|--coverage]` \u003d Same as build but for all projects. If -c, merge zephyr.info files into build/zephyr/all_boards.info\n`testall [-c|--coverage]` \u003d Same as test but for all projects. If -c, merge zephyr.info files into build/zephyr/all_tests.info\n\n`zmake testall` (today) becomes `zmake configureall` --test. `zmake coverage` gets deleted.\n\nOr to be simpler, we could add --all-projects to configure, build, and test.",
